est count, followed by `HALLMARK_APICAL_JUNCTION` and `HALLMARK_ALLOGRAFT_REJECTION`; counts decrease steadily across the remaining Hallmark categories.\nFigure 8 shows a skewed distribution, with hallmark TNFα via NF κ B (302,664) and hallmark UV response DN (205,134) leading, likely due to inflammation and stress studies, boosted by brain and blood tissue dominance (Figure 6). Pathways like hallmark interferonα response (167,957) and hallmark allograft rejection (151,116) follow, reflecting immune biases from lymphoid samples. Rare pathways like hallmark spermatogenesis (3,109) are underrepresented, possibly due to tissue specificity.",
