./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/baseline_vlm_profiles/documents/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000248_de5b21014e76.docling.json:6226:      "orig": "Figure 8 shows a skewed distribution, with hallmark TNF\u03b1 via NF \u03ba B (302,664) and hallmark UV response DN (205,134) leading, likely due to inflammation and stress studies, boosted by brain and blood tissue dominance (Figure 6). Pathways like hallmark interferon\u03b1 response (167,957) and hallmark allograft rejection (151,116) follow, reflecting immune biases from lymphoid samples. Rare pathways like hallmark spermatogenesis (3,109) are underrepresented, possibly due to tissue specificity.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/baseline_vlm_profiles/documents/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000248_de5b21014e76.docling.json:6227:      "text": "Figure 8 shows a skewed distribution, with hallmark TNF\u03b1 via NF \u03ba B (302,664) and hallmark UV response DN (205,134) leading, likely due to inflammation and stress studies, boosted by brain and blood tissue dominance (Figure 6). Pathways like hallmark interferon\u03b1 response (167,957) and hallmark allograft rejection (151,116) follow, reflecting immune biases from lymphoid samples. Rare pathways like hallmark spermatogenesis (3,109) are underrepresented, possibly due to tissue specificity."
